 "_doc": "Curated map from archive slugs (Internet Archive and Common Crawl captures of the firm's own pages) to the base row they name (COLLECTION.md §5: filename and slug variants are fixed in the PARSED SOURCE, not by identity merges). Applied by scratch/wayback-apply-map.py, which sets each parsed row's name to the target row's name so the builder joins them. Renames are the company's own (DriveCam to Lytx, Receipt Bank to Dext, Spot.IM to OpenWeb, Pcysys to Pentera, 360Buy to JD.com, dapulse to monday.com, Eyeblaster to MediaMind, Jirbo to AdColony, Symark to BeyondTrust, Software Technologies Corp to SeeBeyond, AMS to Vertafore, Syncsort to Precisely, PSPDFKit to Nutrient, Episerver to Optimizely, Frontline Education, Instabug to Luciq, SafetyCulture to Mitti, Seevast = Kanoodle's parent renamed, Bestpass to Fleetworthy, CommerceHub to Rithum, Privacera to Trust3 AI, Rattle to Von, Ozsale to Mysale, AutomatedQA to SmartBear, eCommerce Industries = ECi). Written 2026-09-27. Added 2026-09-27 after reading the captured pages: Whitney International University System is Ilumno (the firm's 2017 page for it describes ILUMNO), EPX is Electronic Payment Exchange, LPA Software became Xelus (https://rbj.net/2002/01/25/ex-executives-bid-to-acquire-piece-of-xelus/), candy-capital is the firm's page for Candy Digital. Ecova and Advantage IQ are ENGIE Insight Services (ENGIE bought Ecova in 2014). 'cappella' is the 2008 PHP page for Capella Education (the old site's spelling). 'hundred' is Made For, Inc. (the vitamin brand's company name, PRLog release of 2019). Added after duty 7: the live site keeps these under their later names (Exactera 'formerly known as CrossBorder Solutions'; 'Lantern (fka Employer Direct Healthcare)'), and the firm's /portfolio/micex page became /portfolio/oao-rbc-information-systems-micexrbci in 2023 with the same text, one position. 'nexus-cognitive' is the site row 'Nexus One' (its panel lives at /portfolio/nexus-cognitive/).",
